WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.440
<b>Seiwa</b>

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.440
<b>Fuurin Academy</b>

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.440
<b>Fuurin Academy</b>

00:00:01.190 --> 00:00:02.790
<i>Top of the sixth.</i>

00:00:02.790 --> 00:00:05.260
<i>Seiwa Middle to bat.</i>

00:00:05.260 --> 00:00:08.840
<i>Batting first, second base, Moriguchi-kun.</i>

00:00:08.840 --> 00:00:10.310
<i>Just two innings left...</i>

00:00:10.310 --> 00:00:12.660
<i>Both teams are back to the top of the order.</i>

00:00:12.660 --> 00:00:17.020
<i>The top and bottom of the
sixth will be pivotal in this game.</i>

00:00:18.080 --> 00:00:20.540
Let's clean this up!

00:00:20.870 --> 00:00:24.250
Go, Moriguchi!
Let's do it this inning!

00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:28.590
Right!

00:00:36.220 --> 00:00:38.350
All right! Extra bases!

00:00:38.590 --> 00:00:41.460
Oh no. This is really bad.

00:00:42.140 --> 00:00:43.350
To third! To third!

00:01:06.580 --> 00:01:10.210
S-Safe! Safe!

00:01:10.630 --> 00:01:13.170
Yeah! We took the lead!

00:01:18.540 --> 00:01:20.750
<i>We can't afford to let them get any more runs.</i>

00:01:21.830 --> 00:01:23.430
<i>I need to stop him!</i>

00:01:31.450 --> 00:01:32.530
Anita!

00:01:34.780 --> 00:01:35.570
Second!

00:01:45.300 --> 00:01:47.290
All right! Runners on first and third!

00:01:47.850 --> 00:01:48.970
Anita!

00:01:49.580 --> 00:01:53.250
If she's hurt bad, you won't be able to continue.

00:01:54.200 --> 00:01:57.380
You only have nine players,
which means you have no substitutes,

00:01:57.380 --> 00:02:02.330
and if you can't field another catcher,
you've got no choice but to forfeit the game.

00:02:02.330 --> 00:02:03.290
Do you understand?

00:02:06.170 --> 00:02:07.600
No!

00:02:07.600 --> 00:02:11.270
There's no freakin' way 
we're losin' like this!

00:02:12.330 --> 00:02:13.680
Umpire!

00:02:17.870 --> 00:02:21.450
In that case, I'll switch
from left field to catcher.

00:02:24.530 --> 00:02:27.150
I will be the catcher.

00:03:59.550 --> 00:04:04.390
<b>That Old Daigo Magic?</b>

00:04:05.770 --> 00:04:07.220
Okay, Anita, take it all off.

00:04:07.560 --> 00:04:08.140
Uh...

00:04:08.360 --> 00:04:09.140
Hurry it up.

00:04:09.140 --> 00:04:10.890
Protector and leg guards. Off.

00:04:10.890 --> 00:04:12.360
Oh, right, those.

00:04:12.360 --> 00:04:14.100
What else would he have meant?

00:04:14.480 --> 00:04:18.290
<i>Field change for Fuurin Academy.</i>

00:04:14.730 --> 00:04:16.770
<b>Fujii</b>

00:04:14.730 --> 00:04:16.770
<b>Sagara</b>

00:04:14.730 --> 00:04:16.770
<b>Sawa</b>

00:04:14.730 --> 00:04:16.770
<b>Kabashima</b>

00:04:14.730 --> 00:04:16.770
<b>Sakura</b>

00:04:14.730 --> 00:04:16.770
<b>Kandori</b>

00:04:14.730 --> 00:04:16.770
<b>Nishina</b>

00:04:14.730 --> 00:04:16.770
<b>Tanba</b>

00:04:14.730 --> 00:04:16.770
<b>Shigeno</b>

00:04:16.770 --> 00:04:17.940
<b>Fujii</b>

00:04:16.770 --> 00:04:17.940
<b>Sagara</b>

00:04:16.770 --> 00:04:17.940
<b>Sawa</b>

00:04:16.770 --> 00:04:17.940
<b>Kabashima</b>

00:04:16.770 --> 00:04:17.940
<b>Sakura</b>

00:04:16.770 --> 00:04:17.940
<b>Kandori</b>

00:04:16.770 --> 00:04:17.940
<b>Nishina</b>

00:04:16.770 --> 00:04:17.940
<b>Tanba</b>

00:04:16.770 --> 00:04:17.940
<b>Shigeno</b>

00:04:17.940 --> 00:04:18.480
<b>Fujii</b>

00:04:17.940 --> 00:04:18.480
<b>Sagara</b>

00:04:17.940 --> 00:04:18.480
<b>Sawa</b>

00:04:17.940 --> 00:04:18.480
<b>Kabashima</b>

00:04:17.940 --> 00:04:18.480
<b>Sakura</b>

00:04:17.940 --> 00:04:18.480
<b>Kandori</b>

00:04:17.940 --> 00:04:18.480
<b>Nishina</b>

00:04:17.940 --> 00:04:18.480
<b>Tanba</b>

00:04:17.940 --> 00:04:18.480
<b>Shigeno</b>

00:04:18.290 --> 00:04:21.850
<i>Catcher Kabashima-san
moves to left field.</i>

00:04:18.480 --> 00:04:21.070
<b>Fujii</b>

00:04:18.480 --> 00:04:21.070
<b>Sagara</b>

00:04:18.480 --> 00:04:21.070
<b>Sawa</b>

00:04:18.480 --> 00:04:21.070
<b>Kabashima</b>

00:04:18.480 --> 00:04:21.070
<b>Sakura</b>

00:04:18.480 --> 00:04:21.070
<b>Kandori</b>

00:04:18.480 --> 00:04:21.070
<b>Nishina</b>

00:04:18.480 --> 00:04:21.070
<b>Tanba</b>

00:04:18.480 --> 00:04:21.070
<b>Shigeno</b>

00:04:21.850 --> 00:04:25.530
<i>Left fielder Shigeno-kun
moves to catcher.</i>

00:04:26.950 --> 00:04:27.990
Uh...

00:04:28.890 --> 00:04:31.950
But yer injured too, ain't ya? Yer shoulder...

00:04:32.350 --> 00:04:36.170
Truth is, I hurt my shoulder 
a while back, so I can't take over.

00:04:36.590 --> 00:04:38.660
Sorry for makin' ya do this in yer condition.

00:04:38.660 --> 00:04:40.630
Why are you standing around, Anita?

00:04:40.940 --> 00:04:42.580
Have you taped up your wrist?

00:04:42.580 --> 00:04:44.220
You're covering left field.

00:04:45.090 --> 00:04:46.050
Sawa-san!

00:04:46.050 --> 00:04:48.220
Please tape up Anita's wrist!

00:04:48.220 --> 00:04:49.580
'Kay.

00:04:52.780 --> 00:04:54.890
Pitching warm up. You get two pitches.

00:04:55.190 --> 00:04:58.180
<i>With their catcher injured,
Shigeno's wearing the mask, huh?</i>

00:04:58.480 --> 00:05:03.780
<i>But since he's behind her in the pecking order,
I guess that means he's not as good as her.</i>

00:05:04.150 --> 00:05:05.710
<i>Still, we can't let our guard down.</i>

00:05:06.410 --> 00:05:10.960
<i>He might be a shrimp,
but he knows the game inside out.</i>

00:05:12.590 --> 00:05:14.040
Seriously, Daigo?

00:05:14.620 --> 00:05:18.500
That lie about injuring your shoulder
was painfully transparent.

00:05:20.030 --> 00:05:21.960
Oh, you saw through that?

00:05:22.320 --> 00:05:23.730
Of course I did.

00:05:23.730 --> 00:05:25.300
But why'd you even say that?

00:05:25.300 --> 00:05:28.590
I wanted to get Anita in the
right headspace for catching.

00:05:28.590 --> 00:05:31.580
It looks like it did the trick.

00:05:31.580 --> 00:05:33.660
Well, I guess you're right.

00:05:33.660 --> 00:05:34.680
Anyway...

00:05:38.610 --> 00:05:40.020
Sorry we kept you waiting.

00:05:40.610 --> 00:05:44.570
<i>Batting fourth, catcher, Suzuki-kun.</i>

00:05:45.040 --> 00:05:48.690
<i>They got another run.
No outs, runners on first and third.</i>

00:05:48.690 --> 00:05:52.620
<i>And now, an injured player.
This has "defeat" written all over it.</i>

00:05:53.790 --> 00:05:55.500
<i>All 'cause they won't let me pitch.</i>

00:05:55.960 --> 00:05:56.880
Play!

00:05:59.720 --> 00:06:01.520
<i>Runners, stay put.</i>

00:06:01.520 --> 00:06:05.170
<i>If Urabe steals, and leaves
first open, they'll walk Andy.</i>

00:06:07.290 --> 00:06:11.950
<i>If we just let Andy swing, he'll bring
home the runner on third for sure.</i>

00:06:14.020 --> 00:06:14.810
What?!

00:06:15.500 --> 00:06:16.910
They're walking him?!

00:06:21.910 --> 00:06:23.030
Seriously?

00:06:23.030 --> 00:06:26.070
It's not like first is open...

00:06:30.690 --> 00:06:32.370
What? Intentionally walk him?

00:06:33.410 --> 00:06:34.380
Yeah.

00:06:34.380 --> 00:06:37.540
If they score another run, that's it for us.

00:06:38.050 --> 00:06:40.550
Bases loaded isn't that different
 than first and third.

00:06:41.800 --> 00:06:46.310
Andy's the kind of guy who'll bring the runner
 home even if it results in a double play.

00:06:47.570 --> 00:06:49.990
Best we just avoid taking him on, period.

00:06:51.380 --> 00:06:52.560
You're kidding me.

00:06:52.560 --> 00:06:55.140
Sure, he's their cleanup,
but this is the chicken way out.

00:06:56.560 --> 00:06:59.260
<i>They're doing the worst 
possible thing for us here.</i>

00:07:00.470 --> 00:07:03.810
<i>You're goin' for a mighty
risky play there, Shigeno.</i>

00:07:05.960 --> 00:07:06.780
Ball four!

00:07:09.000 --> 00:07:10.410
Okay!

00:07:15.310 --> 00:07:16.240
B-But...

00:07:17.200 --> 00:07:19.200
With bases loaded,
I might force a run.

00:07:19.580 --> 00:07:20.770
Loading them on purpose...

00:07:20.770 --> 00:07:22.170
Don't sweat it.

00:07:22.760 --> 00:07:26.240
Since the three in the first,
you haven't walked anyone else.

00:07:26.240 --> 00:07:30.300
And anyway, I'd argue they only got those runs
by exploiting weaknesses in our defense.

00:07:33.190 --> 00:07:36.850
<i>Batting fifth, first base, Takahata-kun.</i>

00:07:37.320 --> 00:07:41.470
You and Anita have seriously
done an amazing job so far.

00:07:42.200 --> 00:07:45.180
I know you must be tired from
pitching yesterday and today,

00:07:46.440 --> 00:07:51.280
but keep it up till we're out of this bind,
then we can let our batting do the rest.

00:08:01.200 --> 00:08:02.080
Out!

00:08:04.330 --> 00:08:05.420
Out!

00:08:06.030 --> 00:08:09.130
All <i>right</i>! A 1-2-3 double play!

00:08:10.570 --> 00:08:12.210
Nice, battery!

00:08:12.210 --> 00:08:14.590
Th-That could <i>not</i> have gone any worse!

00:08:16.300 --> 00:08:18.100
Two outs!

00:08:19.740 --> 00:08:23.980
<i>Sakura-senpai was lookin' dog-tired before.
Where'd this second wind come from?</i>

00:08:24.220 --> 00:08:27.940
<i>What's goin' on? What kinda magic </i>is<i> this?</i>

00:08:28.120 --> 00:08:31.290
<i>And wait a minute...
Ain't his shoulder s'posed to be hurt?</i>

00:08:31.290 --> 00:08:34.320
<i>Batting sixth, left field, Hirai-kun.</i>

00:08:34.730 --> 00:08:36.810
Hirai, you gotta step up here!

00:08:36.810 --> 00:08:40.800
Just saying "These things happen" won't cut it
if we don't score after loading the bases.

00:08:44.330 --> 00:08:45.380
Out!

00:08:45.620 --> 00:08:46.880
<b>Seiwa</b>

00:08:45.620 --> 00:08:47.000
<b>Fuurin Academy</b>

00:08:45.620 --> 00:08:47.000
<b>Fuurin Academy</b>

00:08:46.190 --> 00:08:47.330
Three outs!

00:08:47.330 --> 00:08:48.340
Change sides!

00:08:49.770 --> 00:08:50.920
Daigo!

00:08:52.760 --> 00:08:53.200
Nice!

00:08:53.200 --> 00:08:54.420
Nice catch!

00:08:56.120 --> 00:08:56.970
Dammit.

00:08:57.380 --> 00:09:02.430
We took the lead, but that inning's
left a bad taste in our mouth.

00:09:02.920 --> 00:09:06.400
I can't believe Shigeno's gamble paid off.

00:09:07.560 --> 00:09:08.600
<i>Bottom of the sixth.</i>

00:09:08.600 --> 00:09:11.570
<i>Fuurin Academy to bat.</i>

00:09:11.570 --> 00:09:15.030
<i>Batting ninth, catcher, Shigeno-kun.</i>

00:09:15.520 --> 00:09:17.740
Don't let Shigeno get on base.

00:09:18.130 --> 00:09:21.810
If we don't disrupt their momentum,
we'll be in big trouble.

00:09:21.810 --> 00:09:23.670
Yeah, I know.

00:09:23.670 --> 00:09:25.210
Shigeno in particular.

00:09:25.940 --> 00:09:26.830
Play!

00:09:44.180 --> 00:09:45.250
Strike!

00:09:45.250 --> 00:09:46.600
You're out!

00:09:46.600 --> 00:09:48.060
<b>Seiwa</b>

00:09:46.600 --> 00:09:48.100
<b>Fuurin Academy</b>

00:09:46.600 --> 00:09:48.100
<b>Fuurin Academy</b>

00:09:47.270 --> 00:09:48.640
That's game.

00:09:56.790 --> 00:09:59.420
You guys all did so well.

00:09:59.420 --> 00:10:02.240
You lost, sure, but you should
hold your heads up high.

00:10:02.490 --> 00:10:05.100
After all, they say fortune is fickle.

00:10:05.100 --> 00:10:07.210
You get knocked down, you get back up again!

00:10:07.210 --> 00:10:08.620
That's the essence of youth!

00:10:08.620 --> 00:10:10.460
Fight hard for the win again next time!

00:10:10.670 --> 00:10:13.420
Sensei!

00:10:11.580 --> 00:10:13.420
Sensei!

00:10:19.180 --> 00:10:21.230
<i>It's finally over.</i>

00:10:21.230 --> 00:10:24.070
<i>I was afraid I was gonna
lose all three of my days off.</i>

00:10:24.070 --> 00:10:25.050
Foul!

00:10:29.900 --> 00:10:31.830
Are you all right, Sensei?

00:10:31.830 --> 00:10:33.790
Oh, uh, yeah, I-I'm fine.

00:10:34.850 --> 00:10:35.790
Ball!

00:10:37.580 --> 00:10:39.560
I guess it was a dream.

00:10:39.560 --> 00:10:41.730
The game's not over yet.

00:10:42.880 --> 00:10:43.770
Huh?

00:10:43.770 --> 00:10:47.000
It looks like the other
team has taken the lead!

00:10:54.710 --> 00:10:55.680
Foul!

00:10:57.130 --> 00:10:58.960
Nice, nice! That's his tenth pitch!

00:10:58.960 --> 00:11:00.430
You're going strong!

00:11:00.790 --> 00:11:02.720
Captain, you <i>gotta</i> get on base!

00:11:03.040 --> 00:11:04.140
Dammit.

00:11:04.590 --> 00:11:06.100
<i>Shigeno's annoying.</i>

00:11:06.680 --> 00:11:09.060
<i>He's dragging it out, looking for the walk.</i>

00:11:14.640 --> 00:11:17.690
<i>I'm first up this inning at #9,
 with our best batters up next.</i>

00:11:18.130 --> 00:11:20.360
<i>We have to seize the moment 
and turn this game around!</i>

00:11:21.240 --> 00:11:22.160
Center!

00:11:24.980 --> 00:11:25.620
Out!

00:11:29.610 --> 00:11:30.720
Crap.

00:11:30.720 --> 00:11:32.190
Nice, center!

00:11:33.010 --> 00:11:35.170
And that was a good hit too.

00:11:35.170 --> 00:11:39.170
<i>Batting first, center field, Fujii-san.</i>

00:11:40.500 --> 00:11:41.410
<i>All right.</i>

00:11:41.410 --> 00:11:42.970
<i>Just five more outs.</i>

00:11:47.530 --> 00:11:48.390
Ball!

00:11:51.180 --> 00:11:54.690
Since last inning, his curveballs
have stopped finding the zone.

00:11:54.970 --> 00:11:57.770
So let's target his fastball
and hit for contact!

00:12:05.710 --> 00:12:06.830
All right!

00:12:09.240 --> 00:12:10.400
Out!

00:12:10.400 --> 00:12:11.830
Aw, man.

00:12:12.960 --> 00:12:15.290
<i>All righty! Four to go.</i>

00:12:16.410 --> 00:12:19.000
We're staring down the barrel, huh?

00:12:19.200 --> 00:12:22.740
<i>Batting second, shortstop, Sagara-san.</i>

00:12:25.980 --> 00:12:28.140
<i>Two outs, no runners.</i>

00:12:28.340 --> 00:12:30.640
<i>I've got no choice but to go big!</i>

00:12:33.400 --> 00:12:34.560
Go!

00:12:34.560 --> 00:12:35.650
Get outta here!

00:12:40.210 --> 00:12:42.420
Three outs. Change sides!

00:12:52.510 --> 00:12:54.570
<i>I wasn't able to build the
momentum we needed...</i>

00:12:55.350 --> 00:12:56.440
Don't worry!

00:12:56.440 --> 00:12:58.390
We're not done yet!

00:13:00.920 --> 00:13:02.770
What are you doing, Daigo?

00:13:02.770 --> 00:13:04.650
Why don't you have your gear on yet?

00:13:04.650 --> 00:13:06.380
Ah, sorry!

00:13:06.380 --> 00:13:08.270
<i>Top of the seventh.</i>

00:13:08.270 --> 00:13:10.460
<i>Seiwa Middle to bat.</i>

00:13:10.460 --> 00:13:13.780
<i>Batting seventh, right field, Terahara-kun.</i>

00:13:13.780 --> 00:13:15.060
I'm sorry!

00:13:15.610 --> 00:13:16.270
Play!

00:13:18.600 --> 00:13:22.690
<i>I messed up our flow by not getting on base.</i>

00:13:25.510 --> 00:13:26.610
Strike!

00:13:26.800 --> 00:13:29.270
<i>Sawa-san's up in the last, which is good,</i>

00:13:29.270 --> 00:13:31.370
<i>but Anita's hurt her wrist,</i>

00:13:32.300 --> 00:13:34.460
<i>so it's not looking good for us.</i>

00:13:34.870 --> 00:13:36.330
<b>Seiwa</b>

00:13:34.870 --> 00:13:36.330
<b>Fuurin Academy</b>

00:13:34.870 --> 00:13:36.330
<b>Fuurin Academy</b>

00:13:35.290 --> 00:13:37.830
<i>I wanted us to get some
more games under our belt,</i>

00:13:38.640 --> 00:13:43.510
<i>but it seems one win is the best
a rookie team with no coach can manage.</i>

00:13:52.190 --> 00:13:53.620
Hit by pitch!

00:13:54.520 --> 00:13:56.430
I-I'm very sorry!

00:13:57.820 --> 00:14:00.270
All right. Another runner on base!

00:14:00.270 --> 00:14:01.610
<i>Oh no...</i>

00:14:01.610 --> 00:14:04.290
<i>Mutsuko's even more tired than last inning.</i>

00:14:04.290 --> 00:14:07.280
<i>Batting eighth, shortstop, Saito-kun.</i>

00:14:07.280 --> 00:14:09.070
<i>What should I do?</i>

00:14:09.070 --> 00:14:11.190
<i>Mutsuko's pitched back-to-back games.</i>

00:14:11.190 --> 00:14:14.700
<i>Should I switch her out
for Nishina, for her sake?</i>

00:14:19.960 --> 00:14:21.130
Left!

00:14:22.910 --> 00:14:24.540
I got it!

00:14:32.360 --> 00:14:33.680
It got through!

00:14:33.980 --> 00:14:35.770
No way!

00:14:36.220 --> 00:14:38.320
Go! Keep running!

00:14:47.380 --> 00:14:50.070
Sweet. An insurance run.

00:14:50.720 --> 00:14:52.520
T-Two runs behind...

00:14:54.040 --> 00:14:56.440
You went in too hard, Anita.

00:14:56.440 --> 00:15:00.750
There's no need to go rushing in when
there are no outs and a runner on first.

00:15:00.750 --> 00:15:02.310
S-Sorry!

00:15:02.310 --> 00:15:05.000
It's 'cause I ain't played left field before.

00:15:06.620 --> 00:15:08.320
You big idiot.

00:15:08.320 --> 00:15:12.550
We survive bases loaded without
giving up a run, and this dunce does <i>that</i>.

00:15:12.550 --> 00:15:13.720
<b>Seiwa</b>

00:15:12.550 --> 00:15:13.800
<b>Fuurin Academy</b>

00:15:12.550 --> 00:15:13.800
<b>Fuurin Academy</b>

00:15:16.190 --> 00:15:17.270
Ball!

00:15:23.040 --> 00:15:24.940
<i>Mutsuko's at her limit.</i>

00:15:25.930 --> 00:15:29.990
<i>I want to swap her out, but I didn't
get Nishina to warm up his arm at all.</i>

00:15:30.830 --> 00:15:32.680
<i>This is all my fault!</i>

00:15:36.040 --> 00:15:37.230
Ball three!

00:15:37.920 --> 00:15:39.390
Nice!

00:15:39.390 --> 00:15:41.670
You can do it, Mutsuko!

00:15:52.880 --> 00:15:53.750
Ball!

00:15:54.120 --> 00:15:55.340
Ball four!

00:15:57.630 --> 00:15:58.750
Mutsuko!

00:15:59.610 --> 00:16:00.510
Timeout!

00:16:02.310 --> 00:16:03.290
Mutsuko!

00:16:03.910 --> 00:16:06.430
I-I'm fine, I'm fine.

00:16:06.430 --> 00:16:09.100
I just slipped, that's all.

00:16:10.310 --> 00:16:13.570
Sh-Shigeno... Sakura can't keep this up.

00:16:13.570 --> 00:16:14.730
I know.

00:16:16.560 --> 00:16:18.140
Thank you, Mutsuko.

00:16:18.140 --> 00:16:20.010
You did great, pitching for so long.

00:16:20.610 --> 00:16:24.370
I wasn't planning on putting a first-year
on the mound in this tournament,

00:16:24.890 --> 00:16:27.620
but I can't just let you 
destroy yourself out there.

00:16:29.060 --> 00:16:31.300
Umpire, we're changing pitchers.

00:16:31.670 --> 00:16:33.010
Oh boy...

00:16:33.260 --> 00:16:35.700
He's flapping his gums again.

00:16:35.700 --> 00:16:37.760
This whole game's gone turtle.

00:16:37.760 --> 00:16:41.020
We lost because he didn't make
me the ace from the outset.

00:16:41.170 --> 00:16:43.890
You can't win if your captain's a moron.

00:16:43.890 --> 00:16:45.190
Nishina.

00:16:45.720 --> 00:16:47.490
They're calling for you, Nishina.

00:16:47.690 --> 00:16:49.520
They want you to pitch.

00:16:51.530 --> 00:16:52.570
What?!

00:16:52.570 --> 00:16:53.650
For real?!

00:16:55.220 --> 00:16:57.370
So they're letting him pitch now, huh?

00:16:58.150 --> 00:17:01.020
Just what I was waiting for!

00:17:02.460 --> 00:17:03.770
Thanks for taking over.

00:17:03.770 --> 00:17:06.000
Okay. I got this.

00:17:06.790 --> 00:17:08.230
I'm sorry, Nishina.

00:17:08.230 --> 00:17:13.020
I really should've got you to warm up 
your arm when we were on offense.

00:17:13.640 --> 00:17:17.010
It's my fault you have to go in cold.

00:17:17.510 --> 00:17:21.460
Just start with some light throws
so you don't strain your arm.

00:17:21.970 --> 00:17:24.580
We're already two runs behind,
so it's fine if they get hits.

00:17:24.580 --> 00:17:26.400
Don't push yourself too hard.

00:17:26.960 --> 00:17:29.660
Oh, you don't have to worry about me.

00:17:30.320 --> 00:17:33.900
Five pitches is all it takes for me to warm up.

00:17:36.600 --> 00:17:38.480
They switched pitchers.

00:17:38.480 --> 00:17:41.060
I wonder what this guy's pitches are like.

00:17:49.870 --> 00:17:53.300
<i>Batting first, second base, Moriguchi-kun.</i>

00:17:51.540 --> 00:17:52.400
Play!

00:17:53.670 --> 00:17:55.440
Those pitches aren't anything special!

00:17:55.440 --> 00:17:56.980
Go! Go!

00:17:57.970 --> 00:18:00.390
<i>No outs, runners first and second.
Top of the order.</i>

00:18:00.390 --> 00:18:02.630
<i>For now, let's watch out for bunts.</i>

00:18:06.000 --> 00:18:07.990
<i>"Those pitches aren't anything special"?</i>

00:18:10.730 --> 00:18:14.110
<i>'Course they weren't. I was just warming up.</i>

00:18:19.210 --> 00:18:20.910
Strike!

00:18:20.910 --> 00:18:21.910
Damn!

00:18:21.910 --> 00:18:23.370
That's fast.

00:18:23.940 --> 00:18:26.960
Huh. I don't remember
his pitches being <i>that</i> fast.

00:18:29.330 --> 00:18:31.610
<i>His speed and ball rotation
have improved a lot</i>

00:18:31.610 --> 00:18:34.370
<i>since the introductory
game we had a month ago.</i>

00:18:34.880 --> 00:18:39.050
<i>Is Nishina's physical training 
already paying off?</i>

00:18:41.640 --> 00:18:42.870
Hit by pitch!

00:18:43.420 --> 00:18:44.430
Oops?

00:18:46.390 --> 00:18:49.520
Sweet! Bases loaded with no outs again!

00:18:50.400 --> 00:18:53.360
Seriously? You got speed and nothing else!

00:18:53.580 --> 00:18:55.690
How do you even screw up that fast?

00:18:57.400 --> 00:19:01.450
I'm all about the drama, so I put myself
in perilous situations on purpose.

00:19:01.730 --> 00:19:04.910
<i>Batting second, center field, Miyata-kun.</i>

00:19:05.190 --> 00:19:09.260
<i>Even with that fastball,
he's their relief pitcher for a reason.</i>

00:19:09.260 --> 00:19:11.370
<i>I guess he's all speed, no control.</i>

00:19:12.030 --> 00:19:12.920
Play!

00:19:13.090 --> 00:19:15.380
Nishina, keep your head!

00:19:17.290 --> 00:19:18.240
Ball!

00:19:18.770 --> 00:19:20.720
Let's go! Let's go!

00:19:20.940 --> 00:19:23.470
<i>I guess this was just too sudden.</i>

00:19:23.470 --> 00:19:26.970
<i>He's not physically or 
mentally ready for pitching.</i>

00:19:31.880 --> 00:19:33.550
Stop. Stop!

00:19:34.540 --> 00:19:36.190
Close call.

00:19:36.200 --> 00:19:37.780
Nice one, Shigeno!

00:19:39.320 --> 00:19:40.740
Timeout, please.

00:19:40.740 --> 00:19:42.030
<i>Aw heck.</i>

00:19:42.030 --> 00:19:46.200
<i>We're fallin' to pieces 'cause of me.</i>

00:19:50.300 --> 00:19:52.340
Just give it up, Shigeno.

00:19:52.340 --> 00:19:57.380
You put up a good fight for a team with
only nine players, most of them girls.

00:19:57.630 --> 00:19:59.540
Your rhythm's kinda off.

00:19:59.540 --> 00:20:00.340
Huh?

00:20:00.710 --> 00:20:06.180
Maybe try the windup instead of the set.
Should make it easier to find your rhythm.

00:20:07.290 --> 00:20:10.040
The bases are loaded.
There's nowhere for the runners to go.

00:20:10.040 --> 00:20:14.370
Remember what it was like in the bullpen
and try pitching without rushing.

00:20:14.370 --> 00:20:15.150
But...

00:20:16.170 --> 00:20:17.110
It'll be okay.

00:20:18.010 --> 00:20:22.360
Your core's more stable, and your
pitches are already way better.

00:20:22.930 --> 00:20:25.130
They won't be able to hit your fastballs,

00:20:25.130 --> 00:20:26.490
even if they're down the pipe.

00:20:26.900 --> 00:20:29.490
Just trust in yourself
and throw it at my mitt.

00:20:33.130 --> 00:20:34.030
Play!

00:20:43.700 --> 00:20:44.510
Huh?

00:20:46.510 --> 00:20:47.510
What?

00:20:49.220 --> 00:20:51.680
He's not pitching from the set anymore.

00:20:51.680 --> 00:20:54.480
Right. Wait, did that fix his pitching?

00:20:57.340 --> 00:20:58.940
Strike two!

00:21:07.650 --> 00:21:09.310
Strike three!

00:21:09.620 --> 00:21:11.040
Hell yeah!

00:21:13.580 --> 00:21:15.020
Nice pitch!

00:21:18.600 --> 00:21:20.500
Not bad, kid.

00:21:20.840 --> 00:21:22.760
One out!

00:21:23.000 --> 00:21:25.900
<i>Batting third, pitcher, Urabe-kun.</i>

00:21:25.900 --> 00:21:27.010
Dammit.

00:21:28.520 --> 00:21:31.420
A squeeze won't work
with those fastballs.

00:21:31.420 --> 00:21:34.700
I'll just have to rely on the meat
of our order to get a hit.

00:21:37.430 --> 00:21:39.690
Strike! You're out!

00:21:39.690 --> 00:21:40.900
Hell yeah!

00:21:40.920 --> 00:21:42.940
I-I couldn't get near 'em.

00:21:43.210 --> 00:21:44.150
Yeah!

00:21:44.150 --> 00:21:45.820
Two outs!

00:21:45.970 --> 00:21:47.820
This fella ain't bad after all.

00:21:48.210 --> 00:21:51.330
<i>Batting fourth, catcher, Suzuki-kun.</i>

00:21:51.760 --> 00:21:52.850
<i>Just one more.</i>

00:21:53.380 --> 00:21:55.430
<i>If they're only two ahead, there's still hope!</i>

00:21:56.130 --> 00:21:57.500
Strike!

00:22:00.150 --> 00:22:02.050
<i>Please, Nishina!</i>

00:22:02.880 --> 00:22:04.300
<i>Please get us through this!</i>

00:22:04.300 --> 00:22:06.300
Andy, finish it!

00:22:11.260 --> 00:22:13.430
Strike! You're out!

00:22:13.880 --> 00:22:17.270
All right! We survived!

00:22:17.940 --> 00:22:19.190
<b>Seiwa</b>

00:22:17.940 --> 00:22:19.190
<b>Fuurin Academy</b>

00:22:17.940 --> 00:22:19.190
<b>Fuurin Academy</b>

00:22:18.700 --> 00:22:20.400
We have three outs left.

00:22:21.010 --> 00:22:23.520
It's only two runs.
We can make that up in one go!

00:22:23.810 --> 00:22:25.900
Fuurin, fight!

00:22:26.370 --> 00:22:28.430
Yeah!

00:24:00.530 --> 00:24:02.860
It's the last inning and 
they're two runs ahead.

00:24:02.000 --> 00:24:04.250
<b>Seiwa</b>

00:24:02.000 --> 00:24:04.250
<b>Fuurin Academy</b>

00:24:02.000 --> 00:24:04.250
<b>Fuurin Academy</b>

00:24:02.860 --> 00:24:06.250
Urabe has thwarted me all the way,

00:24:06.250 --> 00:24:10.110
but this time, I'm gonna finish it with my bat!

00:24:10.420 --> 00:24:11.970
It ends here, Shigeno.

00:24:11.970 --> 00:24:14.640
I know we go way back,
but that doesn't matter now.

00:24:14.850 --> 00:24:17.810
We're the team that's gonna win
and progress to Regionals!

00:24:17.810 --> 00:24:19.310
I'm <i>definitely</i> hitting this!

00:24:19.310 --> 00:24:20.650
I'll <i>never</i> let you hit it!

00:24:20.650 --> 00:24:22.520
Next time: "Last Inning."

00:24:20.850 --> 00:24:25.020
<b>Last Inning</b>

00:24:22.520 --> 00:24:24.690
Run to the stage of your dreams!
